    "problem_statement": "MCUmgr currently only supports a UART transport that uses the SMP-over-console framing (base64-encoded, with start/end delimiters and a CRC). This is heavier and slower than necessary for binary links. A new MCUmgr UART transport is required that carries the raw binary SMP protocol without base64 encoding, without the extra console framing, and without a CRC \u2014 accepting raw SMP packets directly from the serial link. A matching in-memory dummy variant of this raw transport is required so the raw behaviour can be unit-tested without any real UART: feeding a raw SMP request into the dummy transport must reassemble it, dispatch it to the SMP command handlers, and produce a correctly-formed raw SMP response (correct header op-code/group/sequence/id/version and correct decoded payload) with no base64/CRC processing.",
